# Run the app against the real backend:
#   cp .env.live.example .env
#
# The session then comes from the API: an access token held in memory and an
# httpOnly refresh cookie the browser keeps. The "explore as" role buttons on
# the sign-in screen are a mock-driver affordance and are refused in live mode —
# sign in as a seeded account instead (see the backend's README).
#
# `/api` rather than http://localhost:8080/api, because the dev server proxies
# it: the refresh cookie has to be first-party or a page reload signs you out.
VITE_API_MODE=live
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api

# -- federated sign-in (optional) -----------------------------------------
# Public client ids; must match the backend's GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID / AZURE_AD_CLIENT_ID.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_AZURE_AD_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_AZURE_AD_TENANT_ID=common
